          "explanation": "Employees shown videos framing stress as enhancing reported fewer psychological symptoms and better work performance than those shown debilitating framing. The tempting wrong answer is that it eliminated cortisol -- the lab portion found a more moderate cortisol response, not an absent one. Effects were modest: mindset is a useful lever, not a replacement for fixing a harmful situation or getting help.",
