          "explanation": "Everyone feels anxious sometimes, and a racing heart before a presentation is a normal stress response. What marks a disorder is the pattern: anxiety that is out of proportion to the real risk, persists over weeks or months, is hard to control, and shrinks your life. The tempting wrong answers describe anxiety that is proportionate and time-limited -- uncomfortable, but not a disorder.",
