          "explanation": "Avoidance brings immediate relief, and that relief acts like a reward, strengthening the urge to avoid next time. At the same time, you miss the chance to learn that the feared situation was manageable, so the alarm fires sooner and louder. The tempting wrong answer -- a permanent cortisol change -- sounds scientific but is not the mechanism. The loop is about learning, which is why gradual exposure works.",
