          "explanation": "Like physical fitness, mental health skills fade without use and are easiest to strengthen when things are calm. A light maintenance routine -- a two-minute weekly check-in, practicing skills on ordinary days, and keeping early warning signs current -- helps catch drift early, the same logic as relapse-prevention approaches like MBCT. The tempting wrong answer is stopping entirely because she feels fine; doing everything daily is unsustainable, and a crisis plan costs nothing to keep.",
